{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfHfJimNMounK7LMVhAD5S","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n6\t- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible and accurate**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features and contrastive ordinal learning. On our benchmark, DCOL achieves significantly higher accuracy than binary detection baselines and standard classification approaches. (MVP signal: 78.2% 4-class accuracy with simple RF on Pythia chain)\n11\t\n12\t2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse**: We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) surprisal variance as the strongest depth signal, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), and (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Depth-graduated curation outperforms binary filtering**: Using predicted depth as a continuous quality proxy enables more nuanced data curation — graduated weighting by depth retains high-quality shallow-generation content while down-weighting deeply recursive text, outperforming binary real/synthetic filtering on downstream task quality. (Proof-of-concept scope, ~1 page)\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark (3 models × 3 strategies × 5+ depths), and propose DCOL — a contrastive ordinal learning method with learnable non-uniform margins that captures the actual geometry of recursive degradation. Crucially, we don't just build a classifier — we provide a Depth Degradation Atlas mapping how features evolve across depths, models, and strategies, including the EDD boundary where discrimination saturates.\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning 3 model families and 3 decoding strategies, DCOL achieves X% ordinal depth estimation accuracy (chance=16.7% for 6-class), with cross-model generalization accuracy of Y%, while the best binary detection baseline repurposed for depth estimation achieves only Z%.\"\n25\t\n26\t## Venue Fit Risks\n27\t\n28\t- **Novelty concern**: DCOL is adapted from CLOC (CVPR 2025). Mitigation: novelty emphasis on problem formalization + Atlas + EDD metric; DCOL is framed as a strong method within the framework, not the sole contribution. Three text-specific modifications (strategy-aware margins, surprisal-augmented anchors, non-uniform learned margins) differentiate from direct CLOC transfer.\n29\t- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Mitigation: method (DCOL) + Atlas (scientific contribution) + curation (practical application) = three-line contribution with clear primary/secondary hierarchy.\n30\t- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, wild-data calibration is probed, ecological transfer is future work.\n31\t\n32\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n33\t\n34\t1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation)\n35\t2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → MVP already shows: d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n36\t3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Leave-one-out experiments are core evaluation\n37\t4. \"Non-monotonic degradation (Drayson et al.)?\" → Learnable margins as soft inductive bias; ablation comparing DCOL vs fixed-margin CORAL vs CE loss\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9408cd1f-7ff7-48c2-a196-b643c86530b3","uuid":"f0b879a8-7f3e-4bb8-ae2c-ebf5d7ac0c07","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:31:10.744Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T140607/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible and accurate**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features and contrastive ordinal learning. On our benchmark, DCOL achieves significantly higher accuracy than binary detection baselines and standard classification approaches. (MVP signal: 78.2% 4-class accuracy with simple RF on Pythia chain)\n\n2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse**: We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) surprisal variance as the strongest depth signal, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), and (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies.\n\n3. **Depth-graduated curation outperforms binary filtering**: Using predicted depth as a continuous quality proxy enables more nuanced data curation — graduated weighting by depth retains high-quality shallow-generation content while down-weighting deeply recursive text, outperforming binary real/synthetic filtering on downstream task quality. (Proof-of-concept scope, ~1 page)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n\n- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark (3 models × 3 strategies × 5+ depths), and propose DCOL — a contrastive ordinal learning method with learnable non-uniform margins that captures the actual geometry of recursive degradation. Crucially, we don't just build a classifier — we provide a Depth Degradation Atlas mapping how features evolve across depths, models, and strategies, including the EDD boundary where discrimination saturates.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning 3 model families and 3 decoding strategies, DCOL achieves X% ordinal depth estimation accuracy (chance=16.7% for 6-class), with cross-model generalization accuracy of Y%, while the best binary detection baseline repurposed for depth estimation achieves only Z%.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **Novelty concern**: DCOL is adapted from CLOC (CVPR 2025). Mitigation: novelty emphasis on problem formalization + Atlas + EDD metric; DCOL is framed as a strong method within the framework, not the sole contribution. Three text-specific modifications (strategy-aware margins, surprisal-augmented anchors, non-uniform learned margins) differentiate from direct CLOC transfer.\n- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Mitigation: method (DCOL) + Atlas (scientific contribution) + curation (practical application) = three-line contribution with clear primary/secondary hierarchy.\n- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, wild-data calibration is probed, ecological transfer is future work.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation)\n2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → MVP already shows: d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Leave-one-out experiments are core evaluation\n4. \"Non-monotonic degradation (Drayson et al.)?\" → Learnable margins as soft inductive bias; ablation comparing DCOL vs fixed-margin CORAL vs CE loss\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015enH6SuCDUJx2Nxatygxia","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"OLMo-1B recursive chain benchmark\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"OLMo-1B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"full_4class_acc\": 0.754,\n7\t      \"full_4class_acc_ci\": [\n8\t        0.74,\n9\t        0.768\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"full_mae\": 0.268,\n12\t      \"full_auc_0v1\": 0.994,\n13\t      \"full_auc_1v2\": 0.838,\n14\t      \"full_auc_2v3\": 0.771,\n15\t      \"filtered_4class_acc\": 0.789,\n16\t      \"filtered_4class_acc_ci\": [\n17\t        0.775,\n18\t        0.803\n19\t      ],\n20\t      \"filtered_mae\": 0.225,\n21\t      \"best_model\": \"RandomForest\",\n22\t      \"top_features\": [\n23\t        \"var_surprisal\",\n24\t        \"mean_ppl\",\n25\t        \"p90_ppl\",\n26\t        \"zipf_alpha\",\n27\t        \"mean_surprisal\"\n28\t      ],\n29\t      \"feature_dim\": 19,\n30\t      \"samples_per_depth_per_strategy\": \"~1200\"\n31\t    },\n32\t    \"tables\": [\n33\t      {\n34\t        \"name\": \"Table: OLMo-1B per-strategy 4-class accuracy\",\n35\t        \"rows\": [\n36\t          {\n37\t            \"strategy\": \"nucleus_p0.95\",\n38\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.768,\n39\t            \"mae\": 0.252,\n40\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.995,\n41\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.849,\n42\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.784\n43\t          },\n44\t          {\n45\t            \"strategy\": \"temperature_0.9\",\n46\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.741,\n47\t            \"mae\": 0.281,\n48\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.993,\n49\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.827,\n50\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.758\n51\t          },\n52\t          {\n53\t            \"strategy\": \"topk_50\",\n54\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.752,\n55\t            \"mae\": 0.271,\n56\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.994,\n57\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.839,\n58\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.77\n59\t          }\n60\t        ]\n61\t      }\n62\t    ],\n63\t    \"figures\": [],\n64\t    \"analysis\": \"OLMo结果确认递归退化信号跨模型存在但强度有差异。temperature策略在OLMo上表现最弱， 因为τ=0.9引入的随机性与OLMo自身生成的多样性叠加，模糊了深度信号。 这预示cross-model泛化中OLMo作为held-out时可能是较难的rotation。\\n\\n\\nOLMo-1B在Dolma上训练，分布与Pythia的Pile有差异。Dolma以清洗后的web text为主， 初始生成（depth 0→1）的分布偏移略小于Pythia，导致depth 0v1的AUC微降（0.994 vs 0.998）。 但OLMo的Dolma训练使其对web-text domain更稳定，depth 2v3退化信号略弱（0.771 vs 0.801）， 因为OLMo的生成在浅层更\\\"像人类\\\"，深层退化启动更晚。整体4-class acc低于Pythia约3pp， 符合median档\\\"信号真实但模型间有波动\\\"的预期。var_surprisal仍是最强特征， 但zipf_alpha在OLMo上排名上升——OLMo的tokenizer和训练数据使词频分布对递归深度更敏感。\\n\"\n65\t  },\n66\t  {\n67\t    \"name\": \"GPT-2 XL recursive chain benchmark\",\n68\t    \"description\": \"GPT-2 XL 1.5B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\",\n69\t    \"results\": {\n70\t      \"full_4class_acc\": 0.798,\n71\t      \"full_4class_acc_ci\": [\n72\t        0.785,\n73\t        0.811\n74\t      ],\n75\t      \"full_mae\": 0.218,\n76\t      \"full_auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n77\t      \"full_auc_1v2\": 0.874,\n78\t      \"full_auc_2v3\": 0.812,\n79\t      \"filtered_4class_acc\": 0.831,\n80\t      \"filtered_4class_acc_ci\": [\n81\t        0.818,\n82\t        0.844\n83\t      ],\n84\t      \"filtered_mae\": 0.183,\n85\t      \"best_model\": \"RandomForest\",\n86\t      \"top_features\": [\n87\t        \"var_surprisal\",\n88\t        \"p90_ppl\",\n89\t        \"mean_ppl\",\n90\t        \"mean_surprisal\",\n91\t        \"p75_ppl\"\n92\t      ],\n93\t      \"feature_dim\": 19,\n94\t      \"samples_per_depth_per_strategy\": \"~1200\"\n95\t    },\n96\t    \"tables\": [\n97\t      {\n98\t        \"name\": \"Table: GPT-2 XL per-strategy 4-class accuracy\",\n99\t        \"rows\": [\n100\t          {\n101\t            \"strategy\": \"nucleus_p0.95\",\n102\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.812,\n103\t            \"mae\": 0.204,\n104\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n105\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.885,\n106\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.823\n107\t          },\n108\t          {\n109\t            \"strategy\": \"temperature_0.9\",\n110\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.783,\n111\t            \"mae\": 0.234,\n112\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.997,\n113\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.861,\n114\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.798\n115\t          },\n116\t          {\n117\t            \"strategy\": \"topk_50\",\n118\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.799,\n119\t            \"mae\": 0.217,\n120\t            \"auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n121\t            \"auc_1v2\": 0.876,\n122\t            \"auc_2v3\": 0.815\n123\t          }\n124\t        ]\n125\t      }\n126\t    ],\n127\t    \"figures\": [],\n128\t    \"analysis\": \"GPT-2 XL展现最强的深度信号，符合其作为\\\"能力较弱模型退化更快\\\"的预期。 这对Atlas叙事有利——不同模型的退化速率不同，但模式（monotonic decrease in AUC）一致。 GPT-2 XL的强信号也意味着在cross-model实验中，它作为训练集的一部分会贡献最多信息， 作为held-out测试集则最容易通过gate。\\n\\n\\nGPT-2 XL是collapse文献中最被研究的模型，其WebText训练集相对较小且老旧。 关键：GPT-2 XL的生成能力弱于Pythia和OLMo，递归生成退化更快更明显， 导致相邻深度间的统计差异更大。depth 0v1的AUC（0.998）与Pythia持平， 但depth 1v2（0.874 vs 0.861）和depth 2v3（0.812 vs 0.801）均高于Pythia。 这意味着GPT-2 XL的EDD可能略高于3（但在6-class下仍然depth 4+坍缩）。 4-class acc 0.798略高于Pythia的0.782，因为GPT-2 XL的退化信号更强。 top features排名与Pythia几乎一致，说明var_surprisal作为核心信号具有跨模型稳定性。\\n\"\n129\t  },\n130\t  {\n131\t    \"name\": \"DCOL contrastive ordinal training\",\n132\t    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large编码器 + 多margin N-pair contrastive loss，6-class depth estimation\",\n133\t    \"results\": {\n134\t      \"dcol_6class_acc_pooled\": 0.571,\n135\t      \"dcol_6class_acc_ci\": [\n136\t        0.556,\n137\t        0.586\n138\t      ],\n139\t      \"dcol_mae_6class\": 0.462,\n140\t      \"dcol_4class_acc\": 0.823,\n141\t      \"dcol_4class_acc_ci\": [\n142\t        0.811,\n143\t        0.835\n144\t      ],\n145\t      \"dcol_mae_4class\": 0.192,\n146\t      \"dcol_auc_0v1\": 0.999,\n147\t      \"dcol_auc_1v2\": 0.912,\n148\t      \"dcol_auc_2v3\": 0.856,\n149\t      \"dcol_auc_3v4\": 0.714,\n150\t      \"dcol_auc_4v5\": 0.628,\n151\t      \"best_lr\": 2e-05,\n152\t      \"best_margin_schedule\": \"learned_non_uniform\",\n153\t      \"convergence_epoch\": 7,\n154\t      \"training_hours_actual\": 12.5\n155\t    },\n156\t    \"tables\": [\n157\t      {\n158\t        \"name\": \"Table: DCOL vs RF feature-based, pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies\",\n159\t        \"rows\": [\n160\t          {\n161\t            \"method\": \"DCOL (DeBERTa + contrastive)\",\n162\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n163\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n164\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n165\t            \"mae_4class\": 0.192\n166\t          },\n167\t          {\n168\t            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n169\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n170\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n171\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.778,\n172\t            \"mae_4class\": 0.241\n173\t          },\n174\t          {\n175\t            \"method\": \"CORAL (DeBERTa + fixed margin)\",\n176\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n177\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n178\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.806,\n179\t            \"mae_4class\": 0.211\n180\t          },\n181\t          {\n182\t            \"method\": \"CE (DeBERTa + cross-entropy)\",\n183\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n184\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n185\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.793,\n186\t            \"mae_4class\": 0.224\n187\t          }\n188\t        ]\n189\t      }\n190\t    ],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"DCOL在EDD边界内（depth 0-3）的优势明确，但对depth 4+无能为力。 这支持median叙事：方法有效但有天花板，天花板由信号本身（而非方法）决定。 CORAL作为ablation的中间点（0.538 vs DCOL 0.571 vs CE 0.519）说明 ordinal inductive bias有帮助，learned margins在此基础上进一步提升。 但DCOL vs CORAL仅+3.3pp，说明增益部分来自ordinal structure本身而非contrastive learning独有。\\n\\n\\nDCOL利用DeBERTa编码器从原始文本学习表示，contrastive ordinal loss强制相邻深度的embedding 距离反映实际退化幅度。6-class pooled acc 0.571处于median范围[0.52,0.62]中段。 关键：DCOL相比RF+features的提升集中在depth 1-3的区分（AUC 1v2从0.86→0.91，2v3从0.80→0.86）， 因为contrastive learning能捕捉features无法编码的微妙语义退化模式。 但depth 3v4的AUC仅0.714——刚好在EDD边界上，depth 4v5的0.628接近随机（chance~0.5）。 这证实EDD≈3：DCOL在depth 0-3上显著优于RF，但无法突破depth 3+的信号天花板。 4-class acc 0.823高于RF的0.782（pooled across 3 models），验证了contrastive learning 在EDD内的有效性。non_uniform learned margins优于fixed margins， 因为实际inter-depth距离高度不均匀（depth 0→1远大于depth 2→3）。\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"Leave-one-model-out generalization\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"3个rotation：每次留一个模型族作test，用另外两个训练DCOL\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"rotation_hold_pythia\": {\n199\t        \"train_on\": [\n200\t          \"OLMo-1B\",\n201\t          \"GPT-2 XL\"\n202\t        ],\n203\t        \"test_on\": \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n204\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.483,\n205\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.721,\n206\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.547\n207\t      },\n208\t      \"rotation_hold_olmo\": {\n209\t        \"train_on\": [\n210\t          \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n211\t          \"GPT-2 XL\"\n212\t        ],\n213\t        \"test_on\": \"OLMo-1B\",\n214\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.421,\n215\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.673,\n216\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.601\n217\t      },\n218\t      \"rotation_hold_gpt2xl\": {\n219\t        \"train_on\": [\n220\t          \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n221\t          \"OLMo-1B\"\n222\t        ],\n223\t        \"test_on\": \"GPT-2 XL\",\n224\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.507,\n225\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.748,\n226\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.521\n227\t      },\n228\t      \"cross_model_loo_6class_acc_mean\": 0.47,\n229\t      \"cross_model_loo_6class_acc_std\": 0.036,\n230\t      \"cross_model_loo_4class_acc_mean\": 0.714,\n231\t      \"gate_pass_count\": \"2/3 rotations ≥ 0.45 (6-class), OLMo rotation at 0.421 misses\"\n232\t    },\n233\t    \"tables\": [\n234\t      {\n235\t        \"name\": \"Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results\",\n236\t        \"rows\": [\n237\t          {\n238\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold Pythia\",\n239\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.483,\n240\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.721,\n241\t            \"mae\": 0.547,\n242\t            \"gate_45\": \"PASS\"\n243\t          },\n244\t          {\n245\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold OLMo\",\n246\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.421,\n247\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.673,\n248\t            \"mae\": 0.601,\n249\t            \"gate_45\": \"FAIL\"\n250\t          },\n251\t          {\n252\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold GPT-2 XL\",\n253\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.507,\n254\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.748,\n255\t            \"mae\": 0.521,\n256\t            \"gate_45\": \"PASS\"\n257\t          },\n258\t          {\n259\t            \"rotation\": \"Mean ± std\",\n260\t            \"acc_6class\": \"0.470 ± 0.036\",\n261\t            \"acc_4class\": \"0.714 ± 0.031\",\n262\t            \"mae\": \"0.556 ± 0.033\",\n263\t            \"gate_45\": \"2/3\"\n264\t          }\n265\t        ]\n266\t      }\n267\t    ],\n268\t    \"figures\": [],\n269\t    \"analysis\": \"OLMo rotation的失败需要在论文中诚实报告为limitation。叙事可以是： \\\"跨模型泛化在架构/数据相似的模型间成立，但对训练分布差异大的模型需要域适应\\\"。 4-class acc 0.714 mean说明\\\"在EDD内的粗粒度估计\\\"仍然跨模型可行， 这支持降级后的Claim 1声明。补充feature importance drift分析解释OLMo为什么难。\\n\\n\\n跨模型泛化是median档的核心挑战。mean 6-class acc 0.470处于[0.42,0.52]范围内。 Hold-OLMo是最弱rotation（0.421，未通过0.45 gate）：OLMo在Dolma上训练， 其生成分布与Pile-trained Pythia和WebText-trained GPT-2 XL差异最大。 Pythia和GPT-2 XL都在\\\"early web text\\\"类型数据上训练，彼此更相似， 所以hold-GPT2XL rotation最强（0.507）——Pythia+OLMo的组合已覆盖足够多样性。 Hold-Pythia居中（0.483），因为OLMo+GPT2XL的组合提供了合理的训练分布。 4-class acc均显著高于6-class，再次确认depth 4+的信号不跨模型迁移。 std=0.036反映\\\"有波动\\\"的median特征——不是所有rotation都稳定通过。\\n\"\n270\t  },\n271\t  {\n272\t    \"name\": \"Depth Degradation Atlas\",\n273\t    \"description\": \"9个model×strategy combo的特征单调性分析、EDD计算、跨模型/策略热力图\",\n274\t    \"results\": {\n275\t      \"edd_per_combo\": {\n276\t        \"pythia_nucleus\": 3,\n277\t        \"pythia_temperature\": 3,\n278\t        \"pythia_topk\": 3,\n279\t        \"olmo_nucleus\": 3,\n280\t        \"olmo_temperature\": 2,\n281\t        \"olmo_topk\": 3,\n282\t        \"gpt2xl_nucleus\": 4,\n283\t        \"gpt2xl_temperature\": 3,\n284\t        \"gpt2xl_topk\": 3\n285\t      },\n286\t      \"edd_median\": 3,\n287\t      \"edd_mean\": 3.0,\n288\t      \"edd_min\": 2,\n289\t      \"edd_max\": 4,\n290\t      \"monotonicity_score_top5_mean\": 0.782,\n291\t      \"monotonicity_score_top5_range\": [\n292\t        0.71,\n293\t        0.85\n294\t      ],\n295\t      \"top5_features_by_monotonicity\": [\n296\t        \"var_surprisal\",\n297\t        \"p90_ppl\",\n298\t        \"mean_ppl\",\n299\t        \"zipf_alpha\",\n300\t        \"mean_surprisal\"\n301\t      ],\n302\t      \"feature_monotonicity_var_surprisal\": 0.847,\n303\t      \"feature_monotonicity_p90_ppl\": 0.823,\n304\t      \"feature_monotonicity_mean_ppl\": 0.801,\n305\t      \"feature_monotonicity_zipf_alpha\": 0.768,\n306\t      \"feature_monotonicity_mean_surprisal\": 0.752,\n307\t      \"non_monotonic_combos\": [\n308\t        \"olmo_temperature_depth3→4_mean_ppl\",\n309\t        \"pythia_topk_depth4→5_var_surprisal\"\n310\t      ],\n311\t      \"min_adjacent_auc_within_edd\": 0.771\n312\t    },\n313\t    \"tables\": [\n314\t      {\n315\t        \"name\": \"Table: EDD per model × strategy\",\n316\t        \"rows\": [\n317\t          {\n318\t            \"model\": \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n319\t            \"nucleus\": 3,\n320\t            \"temperature\": 3,\n321\t            \"topk\": 3\n322\t          },\n323\t          {\n324\t            \"model\": \"OLMo-1B\",\n325\t            \"nucleus\": 3,\n326\t            \"temperature\": 2,\n327\t            \"topk\": 3\n328\t          },\n329\t          {\n330\t            \"model\": \"GPT-2 XL\",\n331\t            \"nucleus\": 4,\n332\t            \"temperature\": 3,\n333\t            \"topk\": 3\n334\t          }\n335\t        ]\n336\t      },\n337\t      {\n338\t        \"name\": \"Table: Top-10 feature monotonicity scores (mean across 9 combos)\",\n339\t        \"rows\": [\n340\t          {\n341\t            \"feature\": \"var_surprisal\",\n342\t            \"mono_score\": 0.847,\n343\t            \"rank_stability\": \"1/9 combos rank 1\"\n344\t          },\n345\t          {\n346\t            \"feature\": \"p90_ppl\",\n347\t            \"mono_score\": 0.823,\n348\t            \"rank_stability\": \"6/9 combos rank ≤ 3\"\n349\t          },\n350\t          {\n351\t            \"feature\": \"mean_ppl\",\n352\t            \"mono_score\": 0.801,\n353\t            \"rank_stability\": \"7/9 combos rank ≤ 4\"\n354\t          },\n355\t          {\n356\t            \"feature\": \"zipf_alpha\",\n357\t            \"mono_score\": 0.768,\n358\t            \"rank_stability\": \"5/9 combos rank ≤ 5\"\n359\t          },\n360\t          {\n361\t            \"feature\": \"mean_surprisal\",\n362\t            \"mono_score\": 0.752,\n363\t            \"rank_stability\": \"8/9 combos rank ≤ 6\"\n364\t          }\n365\t        ]\n366\t      }\n367\t    ],\n368\t    \"figures\": [],\n369\t    \"analysis\": \"Atlas是median档下论文的核心贡献。EDD=3的中位数意味着\\\"ordinal depth estimation在4级粒度上可行\\\"， 这本身就是对model collapse社区的直接贡献——之前没有人系统量化\\\"从哪个depth开始区分变得不可能\\\"。 EDD跨combo的变化（2-4）提供了丰富的分析空间：为什么OLMo+temperature最早饱和？ 为什么GPT-2 XL+nucleus能多撑一层？这些问题直接关联模型能力和解码策略的交互效应。 非单调现象（2/9 combos在EDD之后）可以解释为\\\"信号坍缩后的噪声震荡\\\"而非真实的非单调退化。\\n\\n\\nEDD median=3横跨9个combo，但分布有意义的变化。GPT-2 XL nucleus是唯一EDD=4的combo， 因为GPT-2 XL退化最快（前述），nucleus采样保留了最多信号。OLMo temperature是唯一EDD=2的combo， 因为OLMo的生成多样性本就高，叠加temperature的随机性导致depth 2→3的信号就已饱和。 这种跨combo的EDD变化本身就是Atlas的核心科学贡献——EDD不是一个固定常数而是取决于模型能力和解码策略。 top5特征的单调性得分mean 0.782处于[0.7,0.85]范围。var_surprisal最高（0.847）， 因为递归生成使surprisal分布progressively narrowing——这是最稳定的退化信号。 两个非单调combo出现在depth 3→4之后，符合\\\"EDD边界后信号坍缩\\\"的预期。 min_adjacent_auc_within_edd=0.771（出现在OLMo temperature的depth 1v2），处于[0.72,0.80]范围。\\n\"\n370\t  },\n371\t  {\n372\t    \"name\": \"Leave-one-strategy-out robustness\",\n373\t    \"description\": \"3个rotation：每次留一种策略作test，用另外两种训练DCOL\",\n374\t    \"results\": {\n375\t      \"rotation_hold_nucleus\": {\n376\t        \"train_on\": [\n377\t          \"temperature\",\n378\t          \"topk\"\n379\t        ],\n380\t        \"test_on\": \"nucleus\",\n381\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.528,\n382\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.786\n383\t      },\n384\t      \"rotation_hold_temperature\": {\n385\t        \"train_on\": [\n386\t          \"nucleus\",\n387\t          \"topk\"\n388\t        ],\n389\t        \"test_on\": \"temperature\",\n390\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.492,\n391\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.753\n392\t      },\n393\t      \"rotation_hold_topk\": {\n394\t        \"train_on\": [\n395\t          \"nucleus\",\n396\t          \"temperature\"\n397\t        ],\n398\t        \"test_on\": \"topk\",\n399\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.541,\n400\t        \"acc_4class\": 0.798\n401\t      },\n402\t      \"strategy_loo_6class_acc_mean\": 0.52,\n403\t      \"strategy_loo_6class_acc_std\": 0.021\n404\t    },\n405\t    \"tables\": [\n406\t      {\n407\t        \"name\": \"Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results\",\n408\t        \"rows\": [\n409\t          {\n410\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold nucleus\",\n411\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.528,\n412\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.786\n413\t          },\n414\t          {\n415\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold temperature\",\n416\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.492,\n417\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.753\n418\t          },\n419\t          {\n420\t            \"rotation\": \"Hold topk\",\n421\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.541,\n422\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.798\n423\t          },\n424\t          {\n425\t            \"rotation\": \"Mean ± std\",\n426\t            \"acc_6class\": \"0.520 ± 0.021\",\n427\t            \"acc_4class\": \"0.779 ± 0.019\"\n428\t          }\n429\t        ]\n430\t      }\n431\t    ],\n432\t    \"figures\": [],\n433\t    \"analysis\": \"策略泛化比模型泛化容易的结论对论文positioning有利——说明depth信号主要与模型能力相关， 而非解码策略的artifact。这强化了Atlas中\\\"模型能力决定EDD\\\"的叙事。 Hold-temperature的相对弱势可引出discussion：temperature采样作为最\\\"自由\\\"的策略， 其生成文本的统计分布最不受约束，可能需要专门的domain adaptation。\\n\\n\\n策略间泛化优于模型间泛化（mean 0.520 vs 0.470），因为不同解码策略影响的是生成文本的 表面统计特性（多样性、重复率），而递归退化的核心信号（surprisal variance压缩、 perplexity drift）跨策略更稳定。Hold-temperature最弱（0.492）是因为temperature采样 产生的分布与nucleus/topk的截断采样在尾部行为上差异最大——temperature不截断分布， 而是rescale整个logit空间，导致生成文本的统计profile不同。 Hold-topk最强（0.541）是因为topk_50与nucleus_0.95在实际效果上最接近 （都是尾部截断，只是截断方式不同），所以nucleus训练集已包含了大部分topk的信号。 std=0.021远小于cross-model的0.036，说明策略间差异比模型间差异小。\\n\"\n434\t  },\n435\t  {\n436\t    \"name\": \"DeBERTa end-to-end classifier\",\n437\t    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large直接text→6-class depth分类，无手工特征\",\n438\t    \"results\": {\n439\t      \"e2e_6class_acc\": 0.553,\n440\t      \"e2e_6class_acc_ci\": [\n441\t        0.537,\n442\t        0.569\n443\t      ],\n444\t      \"e2e_mae_6class\": 0.478,\n445\t      \"e2e_4class_acc\": 0.809,\n446\t      \"e2e_4class_acc_ci\": [\n447\t        0.796,\n448\t        0.822\n449\t      ],\n450\t      \"e2e_mae_4class\": 0.206,\n451\t      \"e2e_auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n452\t      \"e2e_auc_1v2\": 0.897,\n453\t      \"e2e_auc_2v3\": 0.838,\n454\t      \"e2e_auc_3v4\": 0.698,\n455\t      \"e2e_auc_4v5\": 0.614,\n456\t      \"training_hours\": 9.2,\n457\t      \"best_lr\": 1e-05\n458\t    },\n459\t    \"tables\": [\n460\t      {\n461\t        \"name\": \"Table: End-to-end vs DCOL vs RF\",\n462\t        \"rows\": [\n463\t          {\n464\t            \"method\": \"DCOL (contrastive ordinal)\",\n465\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n466\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n467\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.823\n468\t          },\n469\t          {\n470\t            \"method\": \"DeBERTa E2E (CE)\",\n471\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.553,\n472\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.478,\n473\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.809\n474\t          },\n475\t          {\n476\t            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n477\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n478\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n479\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.778\n480\t          }\n481\t        ]\n482\t      }\n483\t    ],\n484\t    \"figures\": [],\n485\t    \"analysis\": \"DCOL vs E2E仅+1.8pp（6-class），这在median档下说明contrastive ordinal loss的增益 存在但不压倒性。论文需要将此差距诚实报告并通过ablation（plan_010）分解贡献来源。\\n\\n\\nEnd-to-end DeBERTa（CE loss）的6-class acc 0.553略低于DCOL的0.571， 但高于RF+features的0.497。这是median档的典型结果：end-to-end能学到features 无法捕捉的语义退化信号（如coherence loss、topic drift），但没有DCOL的ordinal inductive bias，它在相邻深度的区分上不如DCOL精确——特别是depth 2v3（0.838 vs 0.856） 和depth 3v4（0.698 vs 0.714）的AUC差距。End-to-end不如DCOL的原因是CE loss 将每个class独立对待，不利用ordinal structure，而递归深度本质上是有序的。 但end-to-end优于RF说明原始文本中确实存在features未编码的退化信号。 这对论文叙事的含义：DCOL = end-to-end表示能力 + ordinal structure，两者都有贡献。\\n\"\n486\t  },\n487\t  {\n488\t    \"name\": \"Baseline battery\",\n489\t    \"description\": \"7个baseline：DivEye features回归、perplexity回归、CORAL、CE、zero-shot LLM、binary ensemble、LOKI features\",\n490\t    \"results\": {\n491\t      \"baselines\": {\n492\t        \"diveye_ordinal_regression\": {\n493\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.432,\n494\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.612,\n495\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.698\n496\t        },\n497\t        \"perplexity_regression\": {\n498\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.389,\n499\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.673,\n500\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.651\n501\t        },\n502\t        \"coral_deberta\": {\n503\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n504\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n505\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.806\n506\t        },\n507\t        \"ce_deberta\": {\n508\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n509\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n510\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.793\n511\t        },\n512\t        \"zeroshot_llm_gpt4o\": {\n513\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.287,\n514\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.892,\n515\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.418\n516\t        },\n517\t        \"binary_ensemble_cascade\": {\n518\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.461,\n519\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.574,\n520\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.723\n521\t        },\n522\t        \"loki_features_regression\": {\n523\t          \"acc_6class\": 0.408,\n524\t          \"mae_6class\": 0.641,\n525\t          \"acc_4class\": 0.672\n526\t        }\n527\t      },\n528\t      \"best_baseline\": \"coral_deberta\",\n529\t      \"best_baseline_6class_acc\": 0.538,\n530\t      \"dcol_delta_over_best_baseline_pp\": 3.3,\n531\t      \"dcol_delta_over_best_nonordinal_pp\": 5.2\n532\t    },\n533\t    \"tables\": [\n534\t      {\n535\t        \"name\": \"Table: Full baseline comparison (pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies)\",\n536\t        \"rows\": [\n537\t          {\n538\t            \"method\": \"DCOL (ours)\",\n539\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n540\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n541\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n542\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"+3.3pp\"\n543\t          },\n544\t          {\n545\t            \"method\": \"CORAL (DeBERTa)\",\n546\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n547\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n548\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.806,\n549\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"—\"\n550\t          },\n551\t          {\n552\t            \"method\": \"CE (DeBERTa)\",\n553\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n554\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n555\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.793,\n556\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-1.9pp\"\n557\t          },\n558\t          {\n559\t            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n560\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n561\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n562\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.778,\n563\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-4.1pp\"\n564\t          },\n565\t          {\n566\t            \"method\": \"Binary cascade\",\n567\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.461,\n568\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.574,\n569\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.723,\n570\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-7.7pp\"\n571\t          },\n572\t          {\n573\t            \"method\": \"DivEye features\",\n574\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.432,\n575\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.612,\n576\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.698,\n577\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-10.6pp\"\n578\t          },\n579\t          {\n580\t            \"method\": \"LOKI features\",\n581\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.408,\n582\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.641,\n583\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.672,\n584\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-13.0pp\"\n585\t          },\n586\t          {\n587\t            \"method\": \"Perplexity regression\",\n588\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.389,\n589\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.673,\n590\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.651,\n591\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-14.9pp\"\n592\t          },\n593\t          {\n594\t            \"method\": \"Zero-shot GPT-4o\",\n595\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.287,\n596\t            \"mae_6class\": 0.892,\n597\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.418,\n598\t            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-25.1pp\"\n599\t          }\n600\t        ]\n601\t      }\n602\t    ],\n603\t    \"figures\": [],\n604\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline battery确认DCOL优于所有baseline但优势中等。CORAL作为最强competitor 说明ordinal structure是关键——DCOL的额外+3.3pp来自learned margins和contrastive learning， 但大部分gain来自ordinal formulation本身。这强化median叙事的重心： \\\"ordinal框架是核心贡献，DCOL是该框架下的一个strong实现\\\"。 Zero-shot LLM的失败是一个有趣的negative result，值得在paper中简短讨论。\\n\\n\\nCORAL是最强baseline（0.538），因为它也利用了ordinal structure，与DCOL共享DeBERTa backbone。 DCOL vs CORAL的+3.3pp处于median的[3,7]范围下端，说明DCOL的增量贡献（learnable margins + contrastive loss + strategy conditioning）存在但中等。CE DeBERTa次之（0.519）， 说明DeBERTa的表示能力本身就很强，ordinal bias带来的额外增益约2pp。 DivEye features（0.432）比RF+19 features（0.497）低，因为DivEye的特征是为binary detection 设计的，缺少var_surprisal等对depth敏感的特征。Zero-shot LLM表现最差（0.287，接近 6-class chance 16.7%但显著高于），说明LLM的深度判断能力很弱——深度不是surface-level可感知的属性。 Binary ensemble cascade（先判binary再细分）达到0.461，优于feature regression但弱于 end-to-end方法，因为cascade的error propagation导致浅层误差累积。 DCOL delta +3.3pp在median范围内偏低，叙事需要强调\\\"框架+Atlas\\\"而非\\\"方法突破\\\"。\\n\"\n605\t  },\n606\t  {\n607\t    \"name\": \"DCOL component ablation\",\n608\t    \"description\": \"移除surprisal anchors / learnable margins / strategy conditioning各一个，测量增量贡献\",\n609\t    \"results\": {\n610\t      \"full_dcol\": {\n611\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n612\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.462\n613\t      },\n614\t      \"ablation_no_surprisal_anchors\": {\n615\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.558,\n616\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.475,\n617\t        \"delta_pp\": -1.3\n618\t      },\n619\t      \"ablation_no_learnable_margins\": {\n620\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.547,\n621\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.485,\n622\t        \"delta_pp\": -2.4\n623\t      },\n624\t      \"ablation_no_strategy_conditioning\": {\n625\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.562,\n626\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.469,\n627\t        \"delta_pp\": -0.9\n628\t      },\n629\t      \"ablation_none_of_three\": {\n630\t        \"acc_6class\": 0.531,\n631\t        \"mae_6class\": 0.498,\n632\t        \"delta_pp\": -4.0\n633\t      }\n634\t    },\n635\t    \"tables\": [\n636\t      {\n637\t        \"name\": \"Table: DCOL ablation\",\n638\t        \"rows\": [\n639\t          {\n640\t            \"variant\": \"Full DCOL\",\n641\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n642\t            \"delta\": \"—\"\n643\t          },\n644\t          {\n645\t            \"variant\": \"– strategy conditioning\",\n646\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.562,\n647\t            \"delta\": \"-0.9\"\n648\t          },\n649\t          {\n650\t            \"variant\": \"– surprisal anchors\",\n651\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.558,\n652\t            \"delta\": \"-1.3\"\n653\t          },\n654\t          {\n655\t            \"variant\": \"– learnable margins\",\n656\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.547,\n657\t            \"delta\": \"-2.4\"\n658\t          },\n659\t          {\n660\t            \"variant\": \"– all three (vanilla contrastive)\",\n661\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.531,\n662\t            \"delta\": \"-4.0\"\n663\t          }\n664\t        ]\n665\t      }\n666\t    ],\n667\t    \"figures\": [],\n668\t    \"analysis\": \"每个组件贡献1-2.4pp，没有单一组件是决定性的。这对median叙事的含义： DCOL的三个text-specific modifications各自有小但一致的贡献， 组合起来提供了4pp的总增益。论文应将此framing为\\\"method engineering\\\"而非\\\"method breakthrough\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLearnable margins的消融影响最大（-2.4pp），因为inter-depth距离的非均匀性是 递归退化的核心特征——fixed margins迫使模型假设所有相邻depth等距，这与实际不符。 Surprisal anchors的消融影响次之（-1.3pp），因为var_surprisal是最强特征， 将其嵌入anchor selection有助于contrastive learning聚焦于最有信息量的样本对。 Strategy conditioning影响最小（-0.9pp），因为在pooled setting下策略间差异 已经被训练数据的多样性部分覆盖——conditioning的主要作用是在per-strategy evaluation 上提升，pooled数字上反映较弱。三个组件全部移除等价于vanilla DeBERTa + N-pair loss， acc降至0.531，仍高于CORAL（0.538→此处应低于CORAL），说明N-pair contrastive loss 本身相比CORAL的rank loss有约-0.7pp的差距，三个text-specific modifications 弥补了这个差距并额外提升+4.0pp。\\n\"\n669\t  },\n670\t  {\n671\t    \"name\": \"Depth extension to 5+ generations and EDD analysis\",\n672\t    \"description\": \"Pythia链延伸到depth 5，分析depth 3-5的信号饱和\",\n673\t    \"results\": {\n674\t      \"pythia_extended_auc_3v4\": 0.708,\n675\t      \"pythia_extended_auc_4v5\": 0.621,\n676\t      \"pythia_extended_auc_5v6\": 0.573,\n677\t      \"feature_overlap_depth4_5_bhattacharyya\": 0.82,\n678\t      \"feature_overlap_depth5_6_bhattacharyya\": 0.91,\n679\t      \"edd_pythia_extended\": 3,\n680\t      \"depth4_5_top_feature_rank_change\": \"zipf_alpha从rank 4升至rank 2，var_surprisal从rank 1降至rank 3\"\n681\t    },\n682\t    \"tables\": [\n683\t      {\n684\t        \"name\": \"Table: Extended depth AUC (Pythia, nucleus)\",\n685\t        \"rows\": [\n686\t          {\n687\t            \"pair\": \"0v1\",\n688\t            \"auc\": 0.998\n689\t          },\n690\t          {\n691\t            \"pair\": \"1v2\",\n692\t            \"auc\": 0.861\n693\t          },\n694\t          {\n695\t            \"pair\": \"2v3\",\n696\t            \"auc\": 0.801\n697\t          },\n698\t          {\n699\t            \"pair\": \"3v4\",\n700\t            \"auc\": 0.708\n701\t          },\n702\t          {\n703\t            \"pair\": \"4v5\",\n704\t            \"auc\": 0.621\n705\t          },\n706\t          {\n707\t            \"pair\": \"5v6\",\n708\t            \"auc\": 0.573\n709\t          }\n710\t        ]\n711\t      }\n712\t    ],\n713\t    \"figures\": [],\n714\t    \"analysis\": \"延伸实验定量确认了depth 3是\\\"有效区分边界\\\"——depth 3之后的AUC衰减斜率平缓化， 趋向0.5。这为EDD=3提供了额外的经验支持。Feature rank变化的发现值得在Atlas section 详细讨论，因为它说明\\\"退化不只是'所有特征同步衰减'而是'不同退化阶段的主导信号切换'\\\"。\\n\\n\\n延伸到depth 5-6后，AUC持续下降：3v4=0.708（已低于原EDD阈值0.72），4v5=0.621， 5v6=0.573（接近random的0.5）。Bhattacharyya overlap从depth 4-5的0.82升至depth 5-6的0.91， 说明特征分布高度重叠。EDD仍为3，因为depth 3v4已低于0.72。 有趣的现象：在depth 4+，var_surprisal不再是最区分性特征，因为surprisal的variance 已经被\\\"压缩到底\\\"——所有深层生成文本的surprisal分布都变得窄且相似。 此时zipf_alpha变得相对更区分，因为词频分布的Zipf参数对极深层退化仍有微弱敏感度。 这种feature rank变化是Atlas中一个有价值的发现点。\\n\"\n715\t  },\n716\t  {\n717\t    \"name\": \"Granularity ablation\",\n718\t    \"description\": \"对比binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class分类粒度\",\n719\t    \"results\": {\n720\t      \"binary_acc\": 0.946,\n721\t      \"binary_auc\": 0.983,\n722\t      \"three_class_acc\": 0.867,\n723\t      \"three_class_mae\": 0.141,\n724\t      \"four_class_acc\": 0.823,\n725\t      \"four_class_mae\": 0.192,\n726\t      \"six_class_acc\": 0.571,\n727\t      \"six_class_mae\": 0.462,\n728\t      \"chance_levels\": {\n729\t        \"binary\": 0.5,\n730\t        \"three_class\": 0.333,\n731\t        \"four_class\": 0.25,\n732\t        \"six_class\": 0.167\n733\t      },\n734\t      \"lift_over_chance\": {\n735\t        \"binary\": \"+44.6pp\",\n736\t        \"three_class\": \"+53.4pp\",\n737\t        \"four_class\": \"+57.3pp\",\n738\t        \"six_class\": \"+40.4pp\"\n739\t      }\n740\t    },\n741\t    \"tables\": [\n742\t      {\n743\t        \"name\": \"Table: Granularity ablation (DCOL, pooled)\",\n744\t        \"rows\": [\n745\t          {\n746\t            \"granularity\": \"Binary (0 vs 1+)\",\n747\t            \"acc\": 0.946,\n748\t            \"chance\": 0.5,\n749\t            \"lift_pp\": 44.6\n750\t          },\n751\t          {\n752\t            \"granularity\": \"3-class (0,1,2+)\",\n753\t            \"acc\": 0.867,\n754\t            \"chance\": 0.333,\n755\t            \"lift_pp\": 53.4\n756\t          },\n757\t          {\n758\t            \"granularity\": \"4-class (0,1,2,3+)\",\n759\t            \"acc\": 0.823,\n760\t            \"chance\": 0.25,\n761\t            \"lift_pp\": 57.3\n762\t          },\n763\t          {\n764\t            \"granularity\": \"6-class (0-5)\",\n765\t            \"acc\": 0.571,\n766\t            \"chance\": 0.167,\n767\t            \"lift_pp\": 40.4\n768\t          }\n769\t        ]\n770\t      }\n771\t    ],\n772\t    \"figures\": [],\n773\t    \"analysis\": \"4-class是sweet spot的结论直接支持EDD=3叙事，也回应了reviewer concern \\\"EDD might be low\\\"。 论文可以argue：4-class粒度（0=原始, 1=first gen, 2=second gen, 3+=deep recursive） 在curation场景中已经足够——用户最需要区分的是\\\"原始vs浅层生成vs深层递归\\\"。\\n\\n\\nBinary（depth 0 vs depth 1+）几乎perfect（0.946），因为depth 0→1的gap远大于其他对。 随粒度增加，absolute acc下降但lift over chance先增后减：4-class的lift最高（+57.3pp）， 说明4-class是\\\"信息量/可行性\\\"的最优平衡点。6-class的lift降至+40.4pp， 因为depth 4和depth 5的加入拖累了整体——它们与depth 3高度混淆。 3-class（0,1,2+）的0.867说明\\\"有多深\\\"这个问题在粗粒度上非常可行。 这些数字共同支持论文叙事：ordinal depth estimation在EDD内可行， 推荐4-class作为实际应用的粒度选择，6-class数字仅作为upper bound report。\\n\"\n774\t  },\n775\t  {\n776\t    \"name\": \"Downstream curation proof-of-concept\",\n777\t    \"description\": \"Depth-graduated weighting vs binary filtering，在1B模型fine-tuning上测试\",\n778\t    \"results\": {\n779\t      \"binary_filter_ppl\": 18.72,\n780\t      \"graduated_weighting_ppl\": 18.14,\n781\t      \"no_filter_ppl\": 19.85,\n782\t      \"oracle_depth_weighting_ppl\": 17.91,\n783\t      \"ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_binary_pct\": 3.1,\n784\t      \"ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_nofilter_pct\": 8.6,\n785\t      \"graduated_vs_binary_p_value\": 0.038,\n786\t      \"downstream_task_acc_binary\": 0.724,\n787\t      \"downstream_task_acc_graduated\": 0.731,\n788\t      \"downstream_task_acc_nofilter\": 0.703\n789\t    },\n790\t    \"tables\": [\n791\t      {\n792\t        \"name\": \"Table: Curation comparison\",\n793\t        \"rows\": [\n794\t          {\n795\t            \"method\": \"No filter\",\n796\t            \"ppl\": 19.85,\n797\t            \"task_acc\": 0.703\n798\t          },\n799\t          {\n800\t            \"method\": \"Binary filter (remove synthetic)\",\n801\t            \"ppl\": 18.72,\n802\t            \"task_acc\": 0.724\n803\t          },\n804\t          {\n805\t            \"method\": \"Graduated weighting (predicted depth)\",\n806\t            \"ppl\": 18.14,\n807\t            \"task_acc\": 0.731\n808\t          },\n809\t          {\n810\t            \"method\": \"Oracle weighting (true depth)\",\n811\t            \"ppl\": 17.91,\n812\t            \"task_acc\": 0.738\n813\t          }\n814\t        ]\n815\t      }\n816\t    ],\n817\t    \"figures\": [],\n818\t    \"analysis\": \"3.1%的PPL reduction和p=0.038的显著性在median档下是\\\"正向但不强\\\"的结果。 论文应将此section控制在~1页，framing为proof-of-concept，明确stated limitation： (1) 只在一个model scale上测试，(2) graduated vs binary的差距在error bar内有overlap， (3) curation效果依赖depth prediction质量。\\n\\n\\nGraduated weighting（1/k权重，k=predicted depth+1）的PPL比binary低3.1%， 处于median的[2,5]范围内。p-value=0.038勉强显著（<0.05），但远未达到强显著。 这是因为graduated weighting的优势主要来自对depth 1-2的差异化处理—— binary filter将所有\\\"synthetic\\\"同等对待，而graduated保留了quality尚可的depth 1内容 并只强力down-weight depth 2+。Oracle depth weighting（用真实depth而非predicted） 的PPL=17.91比graduated的18.14低，gap=1.3%说明prediction error（DCOL的misclassification） 确实影响了curation效果，但graduated仍然明显优于binary。 Downstream task acc的差距更小（0.731 vs 0.724），因为PPL的差异在传导到task performance 时会被衰减。在median档下，这个proof-of-concept足以\\\"展示方向\\\"但不能做强声明。\\n\"\n819\t  },\n820\t  {\n821\t    \"name\": \"7B cross-scale probe\",\n822\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B或Llama-3.1-8B生成3层递归链，用小模型训练的DCOL做zero-shot迁移\",\n823\t    \"results\": {\n824\t      \"zero_shot_transfer_4class_acc\": 0.614,\n825\t      \"zero_shot_transfer_6class_acc\": 0.372,\n826\t      \"fine_tuned_on_7b_4class_acc\": 0.791,\n827\t      \"edd_7b_nucleus\": 3,\n828\t      \"edd_7b_temperature\": 2,\n829\t      \"auc_0v1_7b\": 0.989,\n830\t      \"auc_1v2_7b\": 0.824,\n831\t      \"auc_2v3_7b\": 0.741\n832\t    },\n833\t    \"tables\": [\n834\t      {\n835\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-scale transfer (7B)\",\n836\t        \"rows\": [\n837\t          {\n838\t            \"setting\": \"Zero-shot (train on 1-1.5B, test on 7B)\",\n839\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.614,\n840\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.372\n841\t          },\n842\t          {\n843\t            \"setting\": \"Fine-tuned on 7B data\",\n844\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.791,\n845\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.518\n846\t          },\n847\t          {\n848\t            \"setting\": \"1-1.5B in-distribution (reference)\",\n849\t            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n850\t            \"acc_6class\": 0.571\n851\t          }\n852\t        ]\n853\t      }\n854\t    ],\n855\t    \"figures\": [],\n856\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-scale transfer是limitation而非failure。Zero-shot的gap说明需要scale-aware calibration，但fine-tune后的接近恢复说明depth信号是universal的，只是magnitude不同。 论文中这可以framing为future work方向：scale-invariant depth estimation。\\n\\n\\n7B模型的生成质量显著高于1-1.5B模型，导致递归退化信号更弱——更好的模型在浅层 生成\\\"更像人类\\\"的文本，depth信号被压缩。Zero-shot transfer的4-class acc 0.614 远低于in-distribution的0.823，说明1.5B模型上学到的表示不能直接迁移到7B。 这是因为7B模型的\\\"depth 1\\\"文本质量接近1.5B模型的\\\"depth 0\\\"，导致decision boundary错位。 但fine-tune后恢复到0.791，说明depth信号在7B上仍然存在，只是需要recalibration。 EDD在7B上仍为3（nucleus）但temperature降至2，因为7B+temperature的生成多样性 使得depth 2→3就已不可区分。这进一步支持了Atlas中\\\"模型能力越强，EDD越可能降低\\\"的假设。\\n\"\n857\t  },\n858\t  {\n859\t    \"name\": \"Wild-data calibration\",\n860\t    \"description\": \"DCOL depth scores on RedPajama/Dolma vs perplexity/AlignScore质量代理\",\n861\t    \"results\": {\n862\t      \"spearman_dcol_vs_ppl\": 0.341,\n863\t      \"spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore\": 0.283,\n864\t      \"spearman_dcol_vs_ppl_p_value\": 0.002,\n865\t      \"spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore_p_value\": 0.014,\n866\t      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth0\": 0.72,\n867\t      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth1plus\": 0.28,\n868\t      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth3plus\": 0.06\n869\t    },\n870\t    \"tables\": [\n871\t      {\n872\t        \"name\": \"Table: Wild-data correlation with quality proxies\",\n873\t        \"rows\": [\n874\t          {\n875\t            \"proxy\": \"Perplexity (GPT-2)\",\n876\t            \"spearman\": 0.341,\n877\t            \"p_value\": 0.002\n878\t          },\n879\t          {\n880\t            \"proxy\": \"AlignScore\",\n881\t            \"spearman\": 0.283,\n882\t            \"p_value\": 0.014\n883\t          }\n884\t        ]\n885\t      },\n886\t      {\n887\t        \"name\": \"Table: Predicted depth distribution on RedPajama sample\",\n888\t        \"rows\": [\n889\t          {\n890\t            \"depth\": \"0 (human)\",\n891\t            \"pct\": 72\n892\t          },\n893\t          {\n894\t            \"depth\": \"1\",\n895\t            \"pct\": 16\n896\t          },\n897\t          {\n898\t            \"depth\": \"2\",\n899\t            \"pct\": 6\n900\t          },\n901\t          {\n902\t            \"depth\": \"3+\",\n903\t            \"pct\": 6\n904\t          }\n905\t        ]\n906\t      }\n907\t    ],\n908\t    \"figures\": [],\n909\t    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data结果只能作为calibration而非validation。中等相关说明DCOL的depth score 在wild setting下有一定语义一致性，但controlled→wild的gap明显。 论文应将此作为\\\"ecological validity probe\\\"而非core result， 明确声明\\\"controlled setting是primary，wild transfer是future work\\\"。\\n\\nWild data上没有ground-truth depth，只能用proxy验证。Spearman相关0.341（DCOL score vs PPL） 是中等正相关——高DCOL depth score（预测为深层递归）的文本确实倾向于有更高perplexity， 但相关性不强，因为wild data中高PPL的原因很多（不只是递归深度还有domain、quality等）。 AlignScore的相关更弱（0.283），因为AlignScore衡量的是factual consistency而非statistical degradation——递归深度高不一定意味着factually inconsistent。 72%的wild data被scored为depth 0是合理的——大部分web text仍然是人类写的。 6%被scored为depth 3+可能overestimate，因为模型在controlled setting训练， wild data中的低质量人类文本可能被误判为深层递归。 p-values显著但相关系数中等，符合median档\\\"有正向信号但不强\\\"的预期。\\n\"\n910\t  }\n911\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9408cd1f-7ff7-48c2-a196-b643c86530b3","uuid":"da611d86-0875-4a75-b77c-a816f524e3b7","timestamp":"2026-05-14T14:31:11.019Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T140607/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OLMo-1B recursive chain benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"OLMo-1B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_4class_acc\": 0.754,\n      \"full_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.74,\n        0.768\n      ],\n      \"full_mae\": 0.268,\n      \"full_auc_0v1\": 0.994,\n      \"full_auc_1v2\": 0.838,\n      \"full_auc_2v3\": 0.771,\n      \"filtered_4class_acc\": 0.789,\n      \"filtered_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.775,\n        0.803\n      ],\n      \"filtered_mae\": 0.225,\n      \"best_model\": \"RandomForest\",\n      \"top_features\": [\n        \"var_surprisal\",\n        \"mean_ppl\",\n        \"p90_ppl\",\n        \"zipf_alpha\",\n        \"mean_surprisal\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_dim\": 19,\n      \"samples_per_depth_per_strategy\": \"~1200\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: OLMo-1B per-strategy 4-class accuracy\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"nucleus_p0.95\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.768,\n            \"mae\": 0.252,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.995,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.849,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.784\n          },\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"temperature_0.9\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.741,\n            \"mae\": 0.281,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.993,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.827,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.758\n          },\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"topk_50\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.752,\n            \"mae\": 0.271,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.994,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.839,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.77\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OLMo结果确认递归退化信号跨模型存在但强度有差异。temperature策略在OLMo上表现最弱， 因为τ=0.9引入的随机性与OLMo自身生成的多样性叠加，模糊了深度信号。 这预示cross-model泛化中OLMo作为held-out时可能是较难的rotation。\\n\\n\\nOLMo-1B在Dolma上训练，分布与Pythia的Pile有差异。Dolma以清洗后的web text为主， 初始生成（depth 0→1）的分布偏移略小于Pythia，导致depth 0v1的AUC微降（0.994 vs 0.998）。 但OLMo的Dolma训练使其对web-text domain更稳定，depth 2v3退化信号略弱（0.771 vs 0.801）， 因为OLMo的生成在浅层更\\\"像人类\\\"，深层退化启动更晚。整体4-class acc低于Pythia约3pp， 符合median档\\\"信号真实但模型间有波动\\\"的预期。var_surprisal仍是最强特征， 但zipf_alpha在OLMo上排名上升——OLMo的tokenizer和训练数据使词频分布对递归深度更敏感。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GPT-2 XL recursive chain benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-2 XL 1.5B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_4class_acc\": 0.798,\n      \"full_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.785,\n        0.811\n      ],\n      \"full_mae\": 0.218,\n      \"full_auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n      \"full_auc_1v2\": 0.874,\n      \"full_auc_2v3\": 0.812,\n      \"filtered_4class_acc\": 0.831,\n      \"filtered_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.818,\n        0.844\n      ],\n      \"filtered_mae\": 0.183,\n      \"best_model\": \"RandomForest\",\n      \"top_features\": [\n        \"var_surprisal\",\n        \"p90_ppl\",\n        \"mean_ppl\",\n        \"mean_surprisal\",\n        \"p75_ppl\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_dim\": 19,\n      \"samples_per_depth_per_strategy\": \"~1200\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GPT-2 XL per-strategy 4-class accuracy\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"nucleus_p0.95\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.812,\n            \"mae\": 0.204,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.885,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.823\n          },\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"temperature_0.9\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.783,\n            \"mae\": 0.234,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.997,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.861,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.798\n          },\n          {\n            \"strategy\": \"topk_50\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.799,\n            \"mae\": 0.217,\n            \"auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n            \"auc_1v2\": 0.876,\n            \"auc_2v3\": 0.815\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GPT-2 XL展现最强的深度信号，符合其作为\\\"能力较弱模型退化更快\\\"的预期。 这对Atlas叙事有利——不同模型的退化速率不同，但模式（monotonic decrease in AUC）一致。 GPT-2 XL的强信号也意味着在cross-model实验中，它作为训练集的一部分会贡献最多信息， 作为held-out测试集则最容易通过gate。\\n\\n\\nGPT-2 XL是collapse文献中最被研究的模型，其WebText训练集相对较小且老旧。 关键：GPT-2 XL的生成能力弱于Pythia和OLMo，递归生成退化更快更明显， 导致相邻深度间的统计差异更大。depth 0v1的AUC（0.998）与Pythia持平， 但depth 1v2（0.874 vs 0.861）和depth 2v3（0.812 vs 0.801）均高于Pythia。 这意味着GPT-2 XL的EDD可能略高于3（但在6-class下仍然depth 4+坍缩）。 4-class acc 0.798略高于Pythia的0.782，因为GPT-2 XL的退化信号更强。 top features排名与Pythia几乎一致，说明var_surprisal作为核心信号具有跨模型稳定性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DCOL contrastive ordinal training\",\n    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large编码器 + 多margin N-pair contrastive loss，6-class depth estimation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dcol_6class_acc_pooled\": 0.571,\n      \"dcol_6class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.556,\n        0.586\n      ],\n      \"dcol_mae_6class\": 0.462,\n      \"dcol_4class_acc\": 0.823,\n      \"dcol_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.811,\n        0.835\n      ],\n      \"dcol_mae_4class\": 0.192,\n      \"dcol_auc_0v1\": 0.999,\n      \"dcol_auc_1v2\": 0.912,\n      \"dcol_auc_2v3\": 0.856,\n      \"dcol_auc_3v4\": 0.714,\n      \"dcol_auc_4v5\": 0.628,\n      \"best_lr\": 2e-05,\n      \"best_margin_schedule\": \"learned_non_uniform\",\n      \"convergence_epoch\": 7,\n      \"training_hours_actual\": 12.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DCOL vs RF feature-based, pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"DCOL (DeBERTa + contrastive)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n            \"mae_4class\": 0.192\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.778,\n            \"mae_4class\": 0.241\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"CORAL (DeBERTa + fixed margin)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.806,\n            \"mae_4class\": 0.211\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"CE (DeBERTa + cross-entropy)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.793,\n            \"mae_4class\": 0.224\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DCOL在EDD边界内（depth 0-3）的优势明确，但对depth 4+无能为力。 这支持median叙事：方法有效但有天花板，天花板由信号本身（而非方法）决定。 CORAL作为ablation的中间点（0.538 vs DCOL 0.571 vs CE 0.519）说明 ordinal inductive bias有帮助，learned margins在此基础上进一步提升。 但DCOL vs CORAL仅+3.3pp，说明增益部分来自ordinal structure本身而非contrastive learning独有。\\n\\n\\nDCOL利用DeBERTa编码器从原始文本学习表示，contrastive ordinal loss强制相邻深度的embedding 距离反映实际退化幅度。6-class pooled acc 0.571处于median范围[0.52,0.62]中段。 关键：DCOL相比RF+features的提升集中在depth 1-3的区分（AUC 1v2从0.86→0.91，2v3从0.80→0.86）， 因为contrastive learning能捕捉features无法编码的微妙语义退化模式。 但depth 3v4的AUC仅0.714——刚好在EDD边界上，depth 4v5的0.628接近随机（chance~0.5）。 这证实EDD≈3：DCOL在depth 0-3上显著优于RF，但无法突破depth 3+的信号天花板。 4-class acc 0.823高于RF的0.782（pooled across 3 models），验证了contrastive learning 在EDD内的有效性。non_uniform learned margins优于fixed margins， 因为实际inter-depth距离高度不均匀（depth 0→1远大于depth 2→3）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leave-one-model-out generalization\",\n    \"description\": \"3个rotation：每次留一个模型族作test，用另外两个训练DCOL\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rotation_hold_pythia\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"OLMo-1B\",\n          \"GPT-2 XL\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.483,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.721,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.547\n      },\n      \"rotation_hold_olmo\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n          \"GPT-2 XL\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"OLMo-1B\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.421,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.673,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.601\n      },\n      \"rotation_hold_gpt2xl\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n          \"OLMo-1B\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"GPT-2 XL\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.507,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.748,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.521\n      },\n      \"cross_model_loo_6class_acc_mean\": 0.47,\n      \"cross_model_loo_6class_acc_std\": 0.036,\n      \"cross_model_loo_4class_acc_mean\": 0.714,\n      \"gate_pass_count\": \"2/3 rotations ≥ 0.45 (6-class), OLMo rotation at 0.421 misses\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold Pythia\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.483,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.721,\n            \"mae\": 0.547,\n            \"gate_45\": \"PASS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold OLMo\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.421,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.673,\n            \"mae\": 0.601,\n            \"gate_45\": \"FAIL\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold GPT-2 XL\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.507,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.748,\n            \"mae\": 0.521,\n            \"gate_45\": \"PASS\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Mean ± std\",\n            \"acc_6class\": \"0.470 ± 0.036\",\n            \"acc_4class\": \"0.714 ± 0.031\",\n            \"mae\": \"0.556 ± 0.033\",\n            \"gate_45\": \"2/3\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OLMo rotation的失败需要在论文中诚实报告为limitation。叙事可以是： \\\"跨模型泛化在架构/数据相似的模型间成立，但对训练分布差异大的模型需要域适应\\\"。 4-class acc 0.714 mean说明\\\"在EDD内的粗粒度估计\\\"仍然跨模型可行， 这支持降级后的Claim 1声明。补充feature importance drift分析解释OLMo为什么难。\\n\\n\\n跨模型泛化是median档的核心挑战。mean 6-class acc 0.470处于[0.42,0.52]范围内。 Hold-OLMo是最弱rotation（0.421，未通过0.45 gate）：OLMo在Dolma上训练， 其生成分布与Pile-trained Pythia和WebText-trained GPT-2 XL差异最大。 Pythia和GPT-2 XL都在\\\"early web text\\\"类型数据上训练，彼此更相似， 所以hold-GPT2XL rotation最强（0.507）——Pythia+OLMo的组合已覆盖足够多样性。 Hold-Pythia居中（0.483），因为OLMo+GPT2XL的组合提供了合理的训练分布。 4-class acc均显著高于6-class，再次确认depth 4+的信号不跨模型迁移。 std=0.036反映\\\"有波动\\\"的median特征——不是所有rotation都稳定通过。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Depth Degradation Atlas\",\n    \"description\": \"9个model×strategy combo的特征单调性分析、EDD计算、跨模型/策略热力图\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"edd_per_combo\": {\n        \"pythia_nucleus\": 3,\n        \"pythia_temperature\": 3,\n        \"pythia_topk\": 3,\n        \"olmo_nucleus\": 3,\n        \"olmo_temperature\": 2,\n        \"olmo_topk\": 3,\n        \"gpt2xl_nucleus\": 4,\n        \"gpt2xl_temperature\": 3,\n        \"gpt2xl_topk\": 3\n      },\n      \"edd_median\": 3,\n      \"edd_mean\": 3.0,\n      \"edd_min\": 2,\n      \"edd_max\": 4,\n      \"monotonicity_score_top5_mean\": 0.782,\n      \"monotonicity_score_top5_range\": [\n        0.71,\n        0.85\n      ],\n      \"top5_features_by_monotonicity\": [\n        \"var_surprisal\",\n        \"p90_ppl\",\n        \"mean_ppl\",\n        \"zipf_alpha\",\n        \"mean_surprisal\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_monotonicity_var_surprisal\": 0.847,\n      \"feature_monotonicity_p90_ppl\": 0.823,\n      \"feature_monotonicity_mean_ppl\": 0.801,\n      \"feature_monotonicity_zipf_alpha\": 0.768,\n      \"feature_monotonicity_mean_surprisal\": 0.752,\n      \"non_monotonic_combos\": [\n        \"olmo_temperature_depth3→4_mean_ppl\",\n        \"pythia_topk_depth4→5_var_surprisal\"\n      ],\n      \"min_adjacent_auc_within_edd\": 0.771\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: EDD per model × strategy\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n            \"nucleus\": 3,\n            \"temperature\": 3,\n            \"topk\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"OLMo-1B\",\n            \"nucleus\": 3,\n            \"temperature\": 2,\n            \"topk\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"GPT-2 XL\",\n            \"nucleus\": 4,\n            \"temperature\": 3,\n            \"topk\": 3\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Top-10 feature monotonicity scores (mean across 9 combos)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"feature\": \"var_surprisal\",\n            \"mono_score\": 0.847,\n            \"rank_stability\": \"1/9 combos rank 1\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"feature\": \"p90_ppl\",\n            \"mono_score\": 0.823,\n            \"rank_stability\": \"6/9 combos rank ≤ 3\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"feature\": \"mean_ppl\",\n            \"mono_score\": 0.801,\n            \"rank_stability\": \"7/9 combos rank ≤ 4\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"feature\": \"zipf_alpha\",\n            \"mono_score\": 0.768,\n            \"rank_stability\": \"5/9 combos rank ≤ 5\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"feature\": \"mean_surprisal\",\n            \"mono_score\": 0.752,\n            \"rank_stability\": \"8/9 combos rank ≤ 6\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Atlas是median档下论文的核心贡献。EDD=3的中位数意味着\\\"ordinal depth estimation在4级粒度上可行\\\"， 这本身就是对model collapse社区的直接贡献——之前没有人系统量化\\\"从哪个depth开始区分变得不可能\\\"。 EDD跨combo的变化（2-4）提供了丰富的分析空间：为什么OLMo+temperature最早饱和？ 为什么GPT-2 XL+nucleus能多撑一层？这些问题直接关联模型能力和解码策略的交互效应。 非单调现象（2/9 combos在EDD之后）可以解释为\\\"信号坍缩后的噪声震荡\\\"而非真实的非单调退化。\\n\\n\\nEDD median=3横跨9个combo，但分布有意义的变化。GPT-2 XL nucleus是唯一EDD=4的combo， 因为GPT-2 XL退化最快（前述），nucleus采样保留了最多信号。OLMo temperature是唯一EDD=2的combo， 因为OLMo的生成多样性本就高，叠加temperature的随机性导致depth 2→3的信号就已饱和。 这种跨combo的EDD变化本身就是Atlas的核心科学贡献——EDD不是一个固定常数而是取决于模型能力和解码策略。 top5特征的单调性得分mean 0.782处于[0.7,0.85]范围。var_surprisal最高（0.847）， 因为递归生成使surprisal分布progressively narrowing——这是最稳定的退化信号。 两个非单调combo出现在depth 3→4之后，符合\\\"EDD边界后信号坍缩\\\"的预期。 min_adjacent_auc_within_edd=0.771（出现在OLMo temperature的depth 1v2），处于[0.72,0.80]范围。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Leave-one-strategy-out robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"3个rotation：每次留一种策略作test，用另外两种训练DCOL\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rotation_hold_nucleus\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"temperature\",\n          \"topk\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"nucleus\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.528,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.786\n      },\n      \"rotation_hold_temperature\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"nucleus\",\n          \"topk\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"temperature\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.492,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.753\n      },\n      \"rotation_hold_topk\": {\n        \"train_on\": [\n          \"nucleus\",\n          \"temperature\"\n        ],\n        \"test_on\": \"topk\",\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.541,\n        \"acc_4class\": 0.798\n      },\n      \"strategy_loo_6class_acc_mean\": 0.52,\n      \"strategy_loo_6class_acc_std\": 0.021\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold nucleus\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.528,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.786\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold temperature\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.492,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.753\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Hold topk\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.541,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.798\n          },\n          {\n            \"rotation\": \"Mean ± std\",\n            \"acc_6class\": \"0.520 ± 0.021\",\n            \"acc_4class\": \"0.779 ± 0.019\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"策略泛化比模型泛化容易的结论对论文positioning有利——说明depth信号主要与模型能力相关， 而非解码策略的artifact。这强化了Atlas中\\\"模型能力决定EDD\\\"的叙事。 Hold-temperature的相对弱势可引出discussion：temperature采样作为最\\\"自由\\\"的策略， 其生成文本的统计分布最不受约束，可能需要专门的domain adaptation。\\n\\n\\n策略间泛化优于模型间泛化（mean 0.520 vs 0.470），因为不同解码策略影响的是生成文本的 表面统计特性（多样性、重复率），而递归退化的核心信号（surprisal variance压缩、 perplexity drift）跨策略更稳定。Hold-temperature最弱（0.492）是因为temperature采样 产生的分布与nucleus/topk的截断采样在尾部行为上差异最大——temperature不截断分布， 而是rescale整个logit空间，导致生成文本的统计profile不同。 Hold-topk最强（0.541）是因为topk_50与nucleus_0.95在实际效果上最接近 （都是尾部截断，只是截断方式不同），所以nucleus训练集已包含了大部分topk的信号。 std=0.021远小于cross-model的0.036，说明策略间差异比模型间差异小。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DeBERTa end-to-end classifier\",\n    \"description\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large直接text→6-class depth分类，无手工特征\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"e2e_6class_acc\": 0.553,\n      \"e2e_6class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.537,\n        0.569\n      ],\n      \"e2e_mae_6class\": 0.478,\n      \"e2e_4class_acc\": 0.809,\n      \"e2e_4class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.796,\n        0.822\n      ],\n      \"e2e_mae_4class\": 0.206,\n      \"e2e_auc_0v1\": 0.998,\n      \"e2e_auc_1v2\": 0.897,\n      \"e2e_auc_2v3\": 0.838,\n      \"e2e_auc_3v4\": 0.698,\n      \"e2e_auc_4v5\": 0.614,\n      \"training_hours\": 9.2,\n      \"best_lr\": 1e-05\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: End-to-end vs DCOL vs RF\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"DCOL (contrastive ordinal)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.823\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"DeBERTa E2E (CE)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.553,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.478,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.809\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.778\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DCOL vs E2E仅+1.8pp（6-class），这在median档下说明contrastive ordinal loss的增益 存在但不压倒性。论文需要将此差距诚实报告并通过ablation（plan_010）分解贡献来源。\\n\\n\\nEnd-to-end DeBERTa（CE loss）的6-class acc 0.553略低于DCOL的0.571， 但高于RF+features的0.497。这是median档的典型结果：end-to-end能学到features 无法捕捉的语义退化信号（如coherence loss、topic drift），但没有DCOL的ordinal inductive bias，它在相邻深度的区分上不如DCOL精确——特别是depth 2v3（0.838 vs 0.856） 和depth 3v4（0.698 vs 0.714）的AUC差距。End-to-end不如DCOL的原因是CE loss 将每个class独立对待，不利用ordinal structure，而递归深度本质上是有序的。 但end-to-end优于RF说明原始文本中确实存在features未编码的退化信号。 这对论文叙事的含义：DCOL = end-to-end表示能力 + ordinal structure，两者都有贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Baseline battery\",\n    \"description\": \"7个baseline：DivEye features回归、perplexity回归、CORAL、CE、zero-shot LLM、binary ensemble、LOKI features\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baselines\": {\n        \"diveye_ordinal_regression\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.432,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.612,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.698\n        },\n        \"perplexity_regression\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.389,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.673,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.651\n        },\n        \"coral_deberta\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.806\n        },\n        \"ce_deberta\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.793\n        },\n        \"zeroshot_llm_gpt4o\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.287,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.892,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.418\n        },\n        \"binary_ensemble_cascade\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.461,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.574,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.723\n        },\n        \"loki_features_regression\": {\n          \"acc_6class\": 0.408,\n          \"mae_6class\": 0.641,\n          \"acc_4class\": 0.672\n        }\n      },\n      \"best_baseline\": \"coral_deberta\",\n      \"best_baseline_6class_acc\": 0.538,\n      \"dcol_delta_over_best_baseline_pp\": 3.3,\n      \"dcol_delta_over_best_nonordinal_pp\": 5.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Full baseline comparison (pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"DCOL (ours)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.462,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"+3.3pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"CORAL (DeBERTa)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.538,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.491,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.806,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"—\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"CE (DeBERTa)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.519,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.512,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.793,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-1.9pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"RF + 19 features\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.497,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.538,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.778,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-4.1pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Binary cascade\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.461,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.574,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.723,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-7.7pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"DivEye features\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.432,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.612,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.698,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-10.6pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"LOKI features\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.408,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.641,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.672,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-13.0pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Perplexity regression\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.389,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.673,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.651,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-14.9pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Zero-shot GPT-4o\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.287,\n            \"mae_6class\": 0.892,\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.418,\n            \"delta_vs_best\": \"-25.1pp\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline battery确认DCOL优于所有baseline但优势中等。CORAL作为最强competitor 说明ordinal structure是关键——DCOL的额外+3.3pp来自learned margins和contrastive learning， 但大部分gain来自ordinal formulation本身。这强化median叙事的重心： \\\"ordinal框架是核心贡献，DCOL是该框架下的一个strong实现\\\"。 Zero-shot LLM的失败是一个有趣的negative result，值得在paper中简短讨论。\\n\\n\\nCORAL是最强baseline（0.538），因为它也利用了ordinal structure，与DCOL共享DeBERTa backbone。 DCOL vs CORAL的+3.3pp处于median的[3,7]范围下端，说明DCOL的增量贡献（learnable margins + contrastive loss + strategy conditioning）存在但中等。CE DeBERTa次之（0.519）， 说明DeBERTa的表示能力本身就很强，ordinal bias带来的额外增益约2pp。 DivEye features（0.432）比RF+19 features（0.497）低，因为DivEye的特征是为binary detection 设计的，缺少var_surprisal等对depth敏感的特征。Zero-shot LLM表现最差（0.287，接近 6-class chance 16.7%但显著高于），说明LLM的深度判断能力很弱——深度不是surface-level可感知的属性。 Binary ensemble cascade（先判binary再细分）达到0.461，优于feature regression但弱于 end-to-end方法，因为cascade的error propagation导致浅层误差累积。 DCOL delta +3.3pp在median范围内偏低，叙事需要强调\\\"框架+Atlas\\\"而非\\\"方法突破\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DCOL component ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"移除surprisal anchors / learnable margins / strategy conditioning各一个，测量增量贡献\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"full_dcol\": {\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.462\n      },\n      \"ablation_no_surprisal_anchors\": {\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.558,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.475,\n        \"delta_pp\": -1.3\n      },\n      \"ablation_no_learnable_margins\": {\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.547,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.485,\n        \"delta_pp\": -2.4\n      },\n      \"ablation_no_strategy_conditioning\": {\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.562,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.469,\n        \"delta_pp\": -0.9\n      },\n      \"ablation_none_of_three\": {\n        \"acc_6class\": 0.531,\n        \"mae_6class\": 0.498,\n        \"delta_pp\": -4.0\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DCOL ablation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"variant\": \"Full DCOL\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.571,\n            \"delta\": \"—\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"variant\": \"– strategy conditioning\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.562,\n            \"delta\": \"-0.9\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"variant\": \"– surprisal anchors\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.558,\n            \"delta\": \"-1.3\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"variant\": \"– learnable margins\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.547,\n            \"delta\": \"-2.4\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"variant\": \"– all three (vanilla contrastive)\",\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.531,\n            \"delta\": \"-4.0\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"每个组件贡献1-2.4pp，没有单一组件是决定性的。这对median叙事的含义： DCOL的三个text-specific modifications各自有小但一致的贡献， 组合起来提供了4pp的总增益。论文应将此framing为\\\"method engineering\\\"而非\\\"method breakthrough\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLearnable margins的消融影响最大（-2.4pp），因为inter-depth距离的非均匀性是 递归退化的核心特征——fixed margins迫使模型假设所有相邻depth等距，这与实际不符。 Surprisal anchors的消融影响次之（-1.3pp），因为var_surprisal是最强特征， 将其嵌入anchor selection有助于contrastive learning聚焦于最有信息量的样本对。 Strategy conditioning影响最小（-0.9pp），因为在pooled setting下策略间差异 已经被训练数据的多样性部分覆盖——conditioning的主要作用是在per-strategy evaluation 上提升，pooled数字上反映较弱。三个组件全部移除等价于vanilla DeBERTa + N-pair loss， acc降至0.531，仍高于CORAL（0.538→此处应低于CORAL），说明N-pair contrastive loss 本身相比CORAL的rank loss有约-0.7pp的差距，三个text-specific modifications 弥补了这个差距并额外提升+4.0pp。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Depth extension to 5+ generations and EDD analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Pythia链延伸到depth 5，分析depth 3-5的信号饱和\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pythia_extended_auc_3v4\": 0.708,\n      \"pythia_extended_auc_4v5\": 0.621,\n      \"pythia_extended_auc_5v6\": 0.573,\n      \"feature_overlap_depth4_5_bhattacharyya\": 0.82,\n      \"feature_overlap_depth5_6_bhattacharyya\": 0.91,\n      \"edd_pythia_extended\": 3,\n      \"depth4_5_top_feature_rank_change\": \"zipf_alpha从rank 4升至rank 2，var_surprisal从rank 1降至rank 3\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Extended depth AUC (Pythia, nucleus)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"0v1\",\n            \"auc\": 0.998\n          },\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"1v2\",\n            \"auc\": 0.861\n          },\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"2v3\",\n            \"auc\": 0.801\n          },\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"3v4\",\n            \"auc\": 0.708\n          },\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"4v5\",\n            \"auc\": 0.621\n          },\n          {\n            \"pair\": \"5v6\",\n            \"auc\": 0.573\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"延伸实验定量确认了depth 3是\\\"有效区分边界\\\"——depth 3之后的AUC衰减斜率平缓化， 趋向0.5。这为EDD=3提供了额外的经验支持。Feature rank变化的发现值得在Atlas section 详细讨论，因为它说明\\\"退化不只是'所有特征同步衰减'而是'不同退化阶段的主导信号切换'\\\"。\\n\\n\\n延伸到depth 5-6后，AUC持续下降：3v4=0.708（已低于原EDD阈值0.72），4v5=0.621， 5v6=0.573（接近random的0.5）。Bhattacharyya overlap从depth 4-5的0.82升至depth 5-6的0.91， 说明特征分布高度重叠。EDD仍为3，因为depth 3v4已低于0.72。 有趣的现象：在depth 4+，var_surprisal不再是最区分性特征，因为surprisal的variance 已经被\\\"压缩到底\\\"——所有深层生成文本的surprisal分布都变得窄且相似。 此时zipf_alpha变得相对更区分，因为词频分布的Zipf参数对极深层退化仍有微弱敏感度。 这种feature rank变化是Atlas中一个有价值的发现点。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Granularity ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"对比binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class分类粒度\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"binary_acc\": 0.946,\n      \"binary_auc\": 0.983,\n      \"three_class_acc\": 0.867,\n      \"three_class_mae\": 0.141,\n      \"four_class_acc\": 0.823,\n      \"four_class_mae\": 0.192,\n      \"six_class_acc\": 0.571,\n      \"six_class_mae\": 0.462,\n      \"chance_levels\": {\n        \"binary\": 0.5,\n        \"three_class\": 0.333,\n        \"four_class\": 0.25,\n        \"six_class\": 0.167\n      },\n      \"lift_over_chance\": {\n        \"binary\": \"+44.6pp\",\n        \"three_class\": \"+53.4pp\",\n        \"four_class\": \"+57.3pp\",\n        \"six_class\": \"+40.4pp\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Granularity ablation (DCOL, pooled)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"granularity\": \"Binary (0 vs 1+)\",\n            \"acc\": 0.946,\n            \"chance\": 0.5,\n            \"lift_pp\": 44.6\n          },\n          {\n            \"granularity\": \"3-class (0,1,2+)\",\n            \"acc\": 0.867,\n            \"chance\": 0.333,\n            \"lift_pp\": 53.4\n          },\n          {\n            \"granularity\": \"4-class (0,1,2,3+)\",\n            \"acc\": 0.823,\n            \"chance\": 0.25,\n            \"lift_pp\": 57.3\n          },\n          {\n            \"granularity\": \"6-class (0-5)\",\n            \"acc\": 0.571,\n            \"chance\": 0.167,\n            \"lift_pp\": 40.4\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"4-class是sweet spot的结论直接支持EDD=3叙事，也回应了reviewer concern \\\"EDD might be low\\\"。 论文可以argue：4-class粒度（0=原始, 1=first gen, 2=second gen, 3+=deep recursive） 在curation场景中已经足够——用户最需要区分的是\\\"原始vs浅层生成vs深层递归\\\"。\\n\\n\\nBinary（depth 0 vs depth 1+）几乎perfect（0.946），因为depth 0→1的gap远大于其他对。 随粒度增加，absolute acc下降但lift over chance先增后减：4-class的lift最高（+57.3pp）， 说明4-class是\\\"信息量/可行性\\\"的最优平衡点。6-class的lift降至+40.4pp， 因为depth 4和depth 5的加入拖累了整体——它们与depth 3高度混淆。 3-class（0,1,2+）的0.867说明\\\"有多深\\\"这个问题在粗粒度上非常可行。 这些数字共同支持论文叙事：ordinal depth estimation在EDD内可行， 推荐4-class作为实际应用的粒度选择，6-class数字仅作为upper bound report。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Downstream curation proof-of-concept\",\n    \"description\": \"Depth-graduated weighting vs binary filtering，在1B模型fine-tuning上测试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"binary_filter_ppl\": 18.72,\n      \"graduated_weighting_ppl\": 18.14,\n      \"no_filter_ppl\": 19.85,\n      \"oracle_depth_weighting_ppl\": 17.91,\n      \"ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_binary_pct\": 3.1,\n      \"ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_nofilter_pct\": 8.6,\n      \"graduated_vs_binary_p_value\": 0.038,\n      \"downstream_task_acc_binary\": 0.724,\n      \"downstream_task_acc_graduated\": 0.731,\n      \"downstream_task_acc_nofilter\": 0.703\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Curation comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"method\": \"No filter\",\n            \"ppl\": 19.85,\n            \"task_acc\": 0.703\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Binary filter (remove synthetic)\",\n            \"ppl\": 18.72,\n            \"task_acc\": 0.724\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Graduated weighting (predicted depth)\",\n            \"ppl\": 18.14,\n            \"task_acc\": 0.731\n          },\n          {\n            \"method\": \"Oracle weighting (true depth)\",\n            \"ppl\": 17.91,\n            \"task_acc\": 0.738\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3.1%的PPL reduction和p=0.038的显著性在median档下是\\\"正向但不强\\\"的结果。 论文应将此section控制在~1页，framing为proof-of-concept，明确stated limitation： (1) 只在一个model scale上测试，(2) graduated vs binary的差距在error bar内有overlap， (3) curation效果依赖depth prediction质量。\\n\\n\\nGraduated weighting（1/k权重，k=predicted depth+1）的PPL比binary低3.1%， 处于median的[2,5]范围内。p-value=0.038勉强显著（<0.05），但远未达到强显著。 这是因为graduated weighting的优势主要来自对depth 1-2的差异化处理—— binary filter将所有\\\"synthetic\\\"同等对待，而graduated保留了quality尚可的depth 1内容 并只强力down-weight depth 2+。Oracle depth weighting（用真实depth而非predicted） 的PPL=17.91比graduated的18.14低，gap=1.3%说明prediction error（DCOL的misclassification） 确实影响了curation效果，但graduated仍然明显优于binary。 Downstream task acc的差距更小（0.731 vs 0.724），因为PPL的差异在传导到task performance 时会被衰减。在median档下，这个proof-of-concept足以\\\"展示方向\\\"但不能做强声明。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B cross-scale probe\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B或Llama-3.1-8B生成3层递归链，用小模型训练的DCOL做zero-shot迁移\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"zero_shot_transfer_4class_acc\": 0.614,\n      \"zero_shot_transfer_6class_acc\": 0.372,\n      \"fine_tuned_on_7b_4class_acc\": 0.791,\n      \"edd_7b_nucleus\": 3,\n      \"edd_7b_temperature\": 2,\n      \"auc_0v1_7b\": 0.989,\n      \"auc_1v2_7b\": 0.824,\n      \"auc_2v3_7b\": 0.741\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-scale transfer (7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"setting\": \"Zero-shot (train on 1-1.5B, test on 7B)\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.614,\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.372\n          },\n          {\n            \"setting\": \"Fine-tuned on 7B data\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.791,\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.518\n          },\n          {\n            \"setting\": \"1-1.5B in-distribution (reference)\",\n            \"acc_4class\": 0.823,\n            \"acc_6class\": 0.571\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-scale transfer是limitation而非failure。Zero-shot的gap说明需要scale-aware calibration，但fine-tune后的接近恢复说明depth信号是universal的，只是magnitude不同。 论文中这可以framing为future work方向：scale-invariant depth estimation。\\n\\n\\n7B模型的生成质量显著高于1-1.5B模型，导致递归退化信号更弱——更好的模型在浅层 生成\\\"更像人类\\\"的文本，depth信号被压缩。Zero-shot transfer的4-class acc 0.614 远低于in-distribution的0.823，说明1.5B模型上学到的表示不能直接迁移到7B。 这是因为7B模型的\\\"depth 1\\\"文本质量接近1.5B模型的\\\"depth 0\\\"，导致decision boundary错位。 但fine-tune后恢复到0.791，说明depth信号在7B上仍然存在，只是需要recalibration。 EDD在7B上仍为3（nucleus）但temperature降至2，因为7B+temperature的生成多样性 使得depth 2→3就已不可区分。这进一步支持了Atlas中\\\"模型能力越强，EDD越可能降低\\\"的假设。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wild-data calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"DCOL depth scores on RedPajama/Dolma vs perplexity/AlignScore质量代理\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"spearman_dcol_vs_ppl\": 0.341,\n      \"spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore\": 0.283,\n      \"spearman_dcol_vs_ppl_p_value\": 0.002,\n      \"spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore_p_value\": 0.014,\n      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth0\": 0.72,\n      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth1plus\": 0.28,\n      \"pct_wild_data_scored_depth3plus\": 0.06\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Wild-data correlation with quality proxies\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"proxy\": \"Perplexity (GPT-2)\",\n            \"spearman\": 0.341,\n            \"p_value\": 0.002\n          },\n          {\n            \"proxy\": \"AlignScore\",\n            \"spearman\": 0.283,\n            \"p_value\": 0.014\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Predicted depth distribution on RedPajama sample\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"depth\": \"0 (human)\",\n            \"pct\": 72\n          },\n          {\n            \"depth\": \"1\",\n            \"pct\": 16\n          },\n          {\n            \"depth\": \"2\",\n            \"pct\": 6\n          },\n          {\n            \"depth\": \"3+\",\n            \"pct\": 6\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data结果只能作为calibration而非validation。中等相关说明DCOL的depth score 在wild setting下有一定语义一致性，但controlled→wild的gap明显。 论文应将此作为\\\"ecological validity probe\\\"而非core result， 明确声明\\\"controlled setting是primary，wild transfer是future work\\\"。\\n\\nWild data上没有ground-truth depth，只能用proxy验证。Spearman相关0.341（DCOL score vs PPL） 是中等正相关——高DCOL depth score（预测为深层递归）的文本确实倾向于有更高perplexity， 但相关性不强，因为wild data中高PPL的原因很多（不只是递归深度还有domain、quality等）。 AlignScore的相关更弱（0.283），因为AlignScore衡量的是factual consistency而非statistical degradation——递归深度高不一定意味着factually inconsistent。 72%的wild data被scored为depth 0是合理的——大部分web text仍然是人类写的。 6%被scored为depth 3+可能overestimate，因为模型在controlled setting训练， wild data中的低质量人类文本可能被误判为深层递归。 p-values显著但相关系数中等，符合median档\\\"有正向信号但不强\\\"的预期。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":911,"startLine":1,"totalLines":911}}}
